  "Charles Goldfarb",
  "Edward Mosher",
  "Raymond Lorie"
 ],
 "summary": "IBM's Generalized Markup Language: descriptive tags such as :h1., :p., :ol./:li. and :eol. mark the logical role of text, and macro-based \"starter set\" definitions in the SCRIPT/VS formatter of the Document Composition Facility (1978) map them to formatting. GML introduced document types with nested element structure and was the direct predecessor of SGML (ISO 8879).",
 "status": "historical",
 "defined_by": [
  "vendor-specification",
  "reference-implementation"
 ],
